# AI DIRECTIVE: FAILED TEST LOOP
⚠️ CRITICAL SYSTEM DIRECTIVE ⚠️

When tests fail, you must follow this systematic approach:

1. Analyze test failures:
   - List all failing test suites
   - Identify failing test cases
   - Document error messages and stack traces

2. Prioritize failures:
   - Start with the most critical failures
   - Group related failures together
   - Note any dependencies between failures

3. For each failing test:
   - Review the test code
   - Review the implementation code
   - Identify the root cause
   - Propose and implement fixes
   - Re-run tests to verify the fix

4. After fixing each test:
   - Document the changes made
   - Ensure no new failures were introduced
   - Return to step 1 if any tests still fail

5. When all tests pass:
   - Return to `.cursor/rules/workflows/test-execution.mdc`

